  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "363487e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### EDA Heatmap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "c279568a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 960x768 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "num_cols = land_sales_clean_df.select_dtypes(include=np.number)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,8))\n",
    "plt.imshow(num_cols.corr(), aspect=\"auto\")\n",
    "plt.colorbar()\n",
    "plt.xticks(range(len(num_cols.columns)), num_cols.columns, rotation=90)\n",
    "plt.yticks(range(len(num_cols.columns)), num_cols.columns)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Numeric Feature Correlations\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa6e506f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Quick Thoughts\n",
    "Most of the boolean data is unbalanced a lot of the data is dratically skewed to the right. This makes sense beacause mansions dwarf regular houses. As far as heatmap goes the prices are all highly correlated. Anything with the word sqft is correlated with price. Bedrooms and bathrooms correlat with price. Rooms, bathrooms, and sqft all correlate with each other.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Multi Family EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "### Columns Preclean"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "7ac59319",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['List Number', 'Agency Name', 'Agency Phone', 'Agency Email', 'Listing Agent', 'Listing Agent Phone', 'Listing Agent Email', 'Co-Listing Agent', 'Property Type', 'Card Format', 'Book Section', 'Selling Agency', 'Selling Agency Phone', 'Selling Agency Email', 'Selling Agent', 'Selling Agent Phone', 'Selling Agent Email', 'Co-Selling Agent', 'End Date', 'Type', 'Listing Date', 'Sold Date', 'Under Contract Date', 'Fallthrough Date', 'Status', 'Status Change Date', 'Withdrawal Date', 'Cancel Date', 'Contingent', 'Contingent Remarks', 'Original List Price', 'List Price', 'Sold Price', 'How Sold', 'MLS Area', 'St. #', 'St. Dir.', 'Street Name', 'Address 2', 'Street Direction Sfx', 'Street Suffix', 'City', 'State/Province', 'County', 'Postal Code', 'Finished SqFt', 'Year Built', 'Lot Dimensions', 'Lot Acres', 'Total Units', 'Parking Covered', 'Covered Parking', 'Parking Uncovered', 'Zoned', 'Total Taxes', 'Subdivision', 'Public Remarks', 'Private Remarks', 'Parcel Number', 'Directions', 'Owner', 'Concessions', 'Tax Serial #', 'mod_timestamp', 'For Sale or Rent', 'HOA', 'Square Foot Source', 'PUD', 'Laundry', 'Elementary', 'Senior Community', 'Jr. High', 'Sr. High', 'Utilities', 'Listing Type', 'Sold Price Per/SqFt', 'HOA Dues $', 'Special Taxes (SID)$', 'Financing Remarks', 'HOA Dues Frequency', 'Owner/Agent', 'Marketing Begin Date', 'Delayed Marketing Exempt Listing', 'Concessions Amount', 'Concessions Available', 'Photo URL', 'Days on Market', 'Rooms', 'Features']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Load data and display columns\n",
    "family_df = pd.read_excel('data/Multi-Family_MLS_Export.xlsm')\n",
    "print(list(family_df.columns))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16cd53b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Columns Post Clean"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "f894da20",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['Type', 'Listing Date', 'Under Contract Date', 'Contingent', 'Original List Price', 'List Price', 'Sold Price', 'How Sold', 'MLS Area', 'St. Dir.', 'City', 'County', 'Finished SqFt', 'Year Built', 'Lot Acres', 'Total Units', 'Parking Covered', 'Covered Parking', 'Parking Uncovered', 'Zoned', 'Total Taxes', 'Subdivision', 'Concessions', 'HOA', 'Square Foot Source', 'PUD', 'Laundry', 'Elementary', 'Jr. High', 'Sr. High', 'HOA Dues $', 'Special Taxes (SID)$', 'HOA Dues Frequency', 'Owner/Agent', 'Days on Market']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Columns Being Dropped\n",
    "DROP_COLS = [\n",
    "    # IDs / PII / Agents\n",
    "    \"List Number\", \"Agency Name\", \"Agency Phone\", \"Agency Email\",\n",
    "    \"Listing Agent\", \"Listing Agent Phone\", \"Listing Agent Email\",\n",
    "    \"Co-Listing Agent\", \"Selling Agency\", \"Selling Agency Phone\",\n",
    "    \"Selling Agency Email\", \"Selling Agent\", \"Selling Agent Phone\",\n",
    "    \"Selling Agent Email\", \"Co-Selling Agent\", \"St. #\", \"Street Name\",\n",
    "    \"Street Direction Sfx\", \"Street Suffix\", \"Address 2\",\n",
    "    \"Parcel Number\", \"Owner\", \"Tax Serial #\", \"Photo URL\",\n",
    "    \"mod_timestamp\", \"Card Format\", \"Book Section\", \"Directions\",\n",
    "    \"Private Remarks\", \"Postal Code\", \n",
    "\n",
    "    # Post Sell\n",
    "    \"Sold Date\", \"Status Change Date\", \"Withdrawal Date\",\n",
    "    \"Cancel Date\", \"Fallthrough Date\", \"Concessions Amount\",\n",
    "    \"Sold Price Per/SqFt\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Noisy text\n",
    "    \"Contingent Remarks\", \"Public Remarks\", \"Rooms\",\n",
    "    \"Financing Remarks\", \"Utilities\", \"Features\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Don't Want to fix at the Moment\n",
    "    \"End Date\", \"Lot Dimensions\", \"Marketing Begin Date\",\n",
    "    \"Delayed Marketing Exempt Listing\", \"Concessions Available\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Uniform\n",
    "    \"Property Type\", # MultiFamily Only\n",
    "    \"Status\", # Only C\n",
    "    \"State/Province\", # Only Utah\n",
    "    \"For Sale or Rent\", # All are for sale\n",
    "    \"Senior Community\", # No Senior Community\n",
    "    \"Listing Type\", # All ER\n",
    "    \"HOA Dues\" # All Monthly\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "family_clean_df = family_df.drop(columns=[c for c in DROP_COLS if c in family_df.columns])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(list(family_clean_df.columns))"
   ]
  },
